Third-party code carried here so a Mac can fetch its own Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
firmware from Apple's recovery image on the machine itself. Nothing Apple
owns is stored in this repository.

macrecovery.py
  From OpenCorePkg, Utilities/macrecovery, by vit9696 and the Acidanthera
  contributors. BSD 3-Clause License. Talks to Apple's recovery service for
  a board id and verifies the download against its chunklist.
  https://github.com/acidanthera/OpenCorePkg

asahi_firmware/ (core.py, cpio.py, wifi.py, bluetooth.py)
  From the Asahi Linux installer, by The Asahi Linux Contributors. MIT
  License. Turns the firmware tree inside a macOS image into the file names
  the brcmfmac and hci_bcm4377 drivers look for.
  https://github.com/AsahiLinux/asahi-installer

Local change: bluetooth.py imports FWPackage from asahi_firmware.core, as
wifi.py does; upstream's entry point imports it from the package itself,
whose __init__ is empty, so that path fails when run as a module.

